From: Kevin Cahalan <kevinacahalan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: k3: reset a C66x that acknowledged shutdown

k3_rproc_stop() calls notify_shutdown_rproc(), which sends
RP_MBOX_SHUTDOWN, waits for the ACK, and then for the core to report WFI.
On the BeagleBone AI-64 (J721E), a C66x that has sent the ACK and
executed IDLE never reports WFI, so the stop fails with -ETIMEDOUT and
the core cannot be restarted.

A core with a local reset (uses_lreset, the C66x) is safe to hold in
reset once it has acknowledged, so do that when only WFI is missing. A
core that never acknowledged still fails with -EBUSY. The C7x, which has
no local reset, still has to report WFI. The R5F driver has its own
stop and is not affected.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific workaround]
---
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_common.c b/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_common.c
index 9fc5c89..3113003 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_common.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_common.c
@@ -428,7 +428,11 @@ int k3_rproc_stop(struct rproc *rproc)
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = notify_shutdown_rproc(kproc);
-	if (ret)
+	/*
+	 * A C66x never reports WFI, even when it has acknowledged and is
+	 * idle. A core with a local reset is safe to reset anyway.
+	 */
+	if (ret && !(ret == -ETIMEDOUT && kproc->data->uses_lreset))
 		return ret;
 
 	return k3_rproc_reset(kproc);
